.TH GENETREE 1 2000-1月 "parallel_opts" "parallel_opts"
.SH NAME
parallel_opts \- Override the parallelism of a trained model (the perturbation solver) or of a
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIparallel_opts(\fBtree\fR as any, 
\fBthreads\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBthreads_per_model\fR as integer = -1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Override the parallelism of a trained model (the perturbation solver) or of a
 configuration object (the model training).
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBtree\fB \fR\- the GeneTree model or the configuration object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBthreads\fB \fR\- 
 the outer (per gene) degree of parallelism; \fB<= 0\fR restores the automatic mode
 which uses all of the available processors.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBthreads_per_model\fB \fR\- 
 the TGBoost thread number of a single gene model: \fB-1\fR automatic (1 when the genes
 are trained in parallel), \fB0\fR sequential, \fB>0\fR explicit. It only affects the
 model training, it is ignored for the perturbation solving.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the input object with the new parallelism settings.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the training is parallel over the target genes, therefore the per model threads are
 resolved to 1 automatically: nested parallelism (outer over genes plus inner tree
 building) starves the .NET thread pool and the CPU utilization collapses to a few
 cores even on a 128 threads server.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneTree
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
